{#
calendar/_proposal_card.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
A date somebody wrote in a sentence, offered above the mail that said it.

The sibling of _invite_card.html.twig and deliberately close to it: an
invitation and a suggestion are the same shape of thing at the top of a
message, and two cards that looked unrelated would make the second one read as
an advertisement.

Two differences, and both are the point.

The edge is dashed and carries no calendar colour, because nothing has been
added to a calendar yet — an invitation is already an event somewhere, and this
is not. And the sentence it was read from is quoted verbatim. A guess whose
evidence is visible can be judged in a second; a bare date with an Add button
cannot be judged at all, so it gets clicked or ignored on a coin flip.

Rendered from an EventProposal directly rather than through a DTO. There is
nothing to assemble: the row already holds everything the card shows, which is
the difference between this and the invite card — that one has to reconcile an
event, a source link and the account's own addresses.

Variables:
  proposal  EventProposal
#}

<div id="proposal_card_{{ proposal.message.id }}"
     class="mb-4 rounded-pane border border-dashed border-line overflow-hidden">

    <div class="px-4 py-3">

        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <i class="fa-regular fa-calendar-plus mt-0.5 text-ink-faint" aria-hidden="true"></i>

            <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">
                    {{ proposal.title ?: 'calendar.proposal.untitled'|trans }}
                </p>

                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">
                    {% if proposal.isAllDay %}
                        {{ proposal.startsAt|date('D, j M Y') }} · {{ 'calendar.event.all_day'|trans }}
                    {% else %}
                        {{ proposal.startsAt|date('D, j M Y') }} ·
                        {{ proposal.startsAt|date('g:i a') }}–{{ proposal.endsAt|date('g:i a') }}
                    {% endif %}
                </p>

                <p class="text-xs text-ink-faint mt-0.5">
                    {{ 'calendar.proposal.explain'|trans }}
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        {# The evidence. A blockquote rather than a paragraph so it reads as
           somebody else's words, which is exactly what it is. #}
        <blockquote class="mt-3 border-l-2 border-line pl-3 text-xs text-ink-muted italic break-words">
            {{ proposal.sourceSentence }}
        </blockquote>

        {# One form per answer, for the reason the invite card gives: a submit
           button's value only travels when it is the button that was pressed,
           which works until a browser autofills or a script submits the form. #}
        <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <form method="post"
                  action="{{ path('app_calendar_proposal_accept', { id: proposal.message.id }) }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('calendar_proposal' ~ proposal.message.id) }}">

                <button type="submit"
                        class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 h-8 rounded-lg text-xs font-medium transition-colors cursor-pointer bg-accent text-white">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-calendar-plus text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    {{ 'calendar.proposal.action.add'|trans }}
                </button>
            </form>

            <form method="post"
                  action="{{ path('app_calendar_proposal_dismiss', { id: proposal.message.id }) }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('calendar_proposal' ~ proposal.message.id) }}">

                <button type="submit"
                        class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 h-8 rounded-lg text-xs font-medium transition-colors cursor-pointer border border-line text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    {{ 'calendar.proposal.action.dismiss'|trans }}
                </button>
            </form>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
